# Branch settings for Hermit's scripts: KEY=value lines, '#' comments.
#
# The landing branch is the branch changes land on: the merge queue's base,
# the branch validation measures a checkout against, and (for Reverie) the
# history a Hermit Reverie pin must be on. The upstream branch is the
# fast-forward-only inbox that mirrors facebookexperimental. They are separate
# settings even while both name main.
#
# A script reads the environment variable named after the key first, then this
# file. There is no built-in default: a missing, empty, repeated or malformed
# setting is refused, never replaced by main. The readers are
# scripts/lib/landing_branch.sh, ci/manifest-plan/src/landing_branch.rs and
# scripts/landing_branch.py, and they implement the same rule.
#
# The landing-branch flip is done by EDITING this file. Exporting
# HERMIT_LANDING_BRANCH or REVERIE_LANDING_BRANCH alone does not reach every
# consumer: the pinned-root runner (ci/hermetic/run-in-pinned-root.sh)
# forwards only the fixed list of environment variables its --env options
# name, and that list does not include these, so scripts it runs read this
# file. The variables only override the file for a single run outside it.
HERMIT_LANDING_BRANCH=main
REVERIE_LANDING_BRANCH=main
HERMIT_UPSTREAM_BRANCH=main
